WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.840
Hey!

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.050
Māmane!

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.140
Satoshi! Go!
It’s been a while!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.770
Māmane! Togedemaru!
You been doing good?

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.440
Denryu!

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.690
Denryu! Light Pokémon!
Electric type!

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.740
The tail’s tip shines brightly,
and acts as a beacon for lost people!

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:57.330
It’s also famous for being used as
a lighthouse beacon to keep ships safe!

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.960
So it’s here for the project?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.120
Yeah!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.460
Come on, I’ll introduce you.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.510
A-Ahh! Sorry!

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.180
It’s a little scatterbrained...

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.470
Y-You don’t say...

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.220
I’ll be fine...

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.560
Nice to meet you, Denryu.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.730
This is Sarunori.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.690
Nice to meet you,
Sarunori.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.690
Everyone in Alola
doing good, too?

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.820
Of course!

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.740
They’re all dying to see you!

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.740
Kaki even said he wants
another match with you, Go!

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.200
Oh, where’s Rabbifoot?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.990
Come on out!

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.590
Aceburn!

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.630
Rabbifoot’s evolved form!

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.300
Wow! That’s so cool!

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.800
So, ready to go?

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.260
Into the Tokusane Space Center!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.410
Satoshi and Go have arrived at
the Tokusane Space Center in Hoenn.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:46.410
What could they have
planned for today with Māmane...?

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.290
Whoa... Cool...

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.920
Thank you so much for inviting us,
Māmane! This is the best!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.800
W-Well... Yeah...

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.800
Ooh, what’s that?

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.590
Hey, Satoshi!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.550
You’ll get lost
if we don’t stick together!

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:08.350
But yeah, I never imagined you’d be working
on that Fiarrow2 return project...

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.560
I know!
I still feel like I’m dreaming!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.300
So these are your guests,
Māmane?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.210
Yes!

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.340
I’m Satoshi!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.340
My name’s Go!
Thank you for having us.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.050
Welcome.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.470
My name’s Hirota,
I’m a researcher here.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.060
Thank you very much for letting us
come and watch today!

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:50.140
I can’t believe we get to see one of
the century’s biggest projects up close!

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.440
It’s amazing to think there’s Fiarrow
out in space of all places!

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.280
No, there aren’t.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.610
It’s the name of
an asteroid explorer.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.950
Huh? Really?!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.000
Fiarrow2 was launched from right here
at Tokusane Space Center,

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.040
with the mission to
probe an asteroid!

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.800
Here’s some footage
from the launch.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.770
It’s so cool...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:47.910
Fiarrow2 detached from the rocket,
and set off toward its target.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.920
After a very long time,
it landed on the asteroid.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.220
It successfully completed
its mission.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.270
And right now,
it’s in the midst of heading back home.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.520
Which is where
Denryu comes in!

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.530
The light from Denryu’s tail
has a special wavelength.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.900
We’re going to amplify it
and beam it out!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:29.450
And Fiarrow2 has
a light receptor fitted to it.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:35.170
That light will guide it straight back home,
and prevent it from getting lost in the depths of space.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:41.590
In other words, the light from Denryu’s tail
is working like a lighthouse beacon, right?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:44.550
So it’s not just a sea lighthouse,
but a space lighthouse, too!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.970
Since we want to drum up
interest in the study of outer space,

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.310
we let children from all over the world
help with this project.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.890
Ooh, there’s lots of them!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.400
Aw! If only I had a Denryu!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.900
Now, it’s almost time to begin.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.780
Māmane, Denryu,
can you get yourselves ready?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.410
Yes!

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.490
Come on, Denryu!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.510
A-A-Are you all okay?!

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:38.270
A-Anyway,
just get into position for now.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.490
Is this really going to work...?

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:48.610
You got this, Denryu!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.170
Line connection complete!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.920
Begin countdown to switchover
from Kleiber Observatory.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:14.430
17, 16, 15, 14, 13, 12, 11...

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:07.590
Here we go, Denryu!

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.800
Light, on!

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:21.690
10, 9, 8, 7, 6...

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.310
Illumination angle at -0.2.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.020
Output power at 80%.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.440
Illumination from
Kleiber Observatory ending now.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:28.320
3, 2, 1...

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:28.320
Tokusane Space Center
will take over.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:28.950
Illuminate!

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.380
Contact with Fiarrow2 confirmed.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.220
All systems normal.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.680
I don’t know what’s going on,
but wow!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.970
I can’t believe
I’m watching this up close!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.680
That’s it, Denryu!

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:03.940
What?!

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:13.200
Emergency shutdown!

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.240
Ask Aeneas Observatory
to take over ASAP!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.000
On it!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.590
Status?

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:29.760
All systems normal with illumination
from Aeneas Observatory!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.260
Fiarrow2 navigation is on course!

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.810
They did it in time...

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.730
Did we do something wrong...?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.650
Sorry about that.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:51.150
We’ll have it fixed for the next illumination,
so why don’t you let Denryu have a little rest?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:52.740
Sure...

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.600
Denryu, you were amazing!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:23.600
They had some malfunctions,
but your light reached Fiarrow2!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.900
Yeah! It shined out really bright,
like “whoosh!”

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.820
Mr. Hirota and crew
will fix the machine.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.400
Then you can just give it
another try!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.450
Yeah. Thanks.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.580
Denryu. Light, on.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.420
Huh?

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.710
Does that mean...?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.920
It can’t turn its light on
anymore?

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.470
What happened?

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.680
It was shining so bright earlier...

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:04.850
Hmm...

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.440
Maybe it fell into a slump
from the shock of failing?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:15.450
Denryu. If you just relax,
I’m sure you can do it again.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.290
D-D-Denryu?

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.500
Denryu!

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.250
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.050
Denryu!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.930
It’s not here...

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.270
I knew I wasn’t
the right person for this...

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.020
Māmane?

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:53.360
Since I’m not Denryu’s trainer...

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:56.360
Huh? You didn’t catch it, Māmane?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.490
Right.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:02.330
I borrowed it from Big Mu
to take part in the project.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:03.700
Big Mu?

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.250
Oh, Mr. Mullein
from Hokulani Observatory.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.870
Māmane’s cousin.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:17.880
I wanted to take part really bad,
so I asked Big Mu and borrowed his Denryu.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:22.810
They invited me here to the
Tokusane Space Center because of Denryu...

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:26.730
So I really wanted
to make this a success.

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.020
Māmane...

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:34.780
I can’t do anything to cheer up Denryu,
so I’m just a nuisance to everyone else...

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:38.990
I should never
have accepted the invitation...

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:40.490
Don’t think like that!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.570
Satoshi?

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.660
You’re always trying your hardest,
going at full power!

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:49.420
You even came here today
‘cause your dream’s to be an astronaut, right?

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.130
Yeah.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.340
So give it your full power
till the very end!

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.420
He’s right!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.800
It’s not over yet!

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:00.470
And that’s why
we need to find Denryu!

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:01.640
Huh?

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:02.890
Where’s Sarunori?

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:09.690
Sarunori’s disappeared, too!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.060
Well, knowing Sarunori...

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:17.480
...it might’ve gone chasing after something
thinking it was Denryu’s light.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.340
Sarunori!

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.500
Denryu!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.840
Hey! Where are you?!

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:48.810
Denryu!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.520
What a relief...

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:54.100
That just leaves Sarunori.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.650
The weather’s not looking good.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:13:59.900
That’s it!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.280
Togedemaru, light!

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.950
No good...

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.620
It’s not enough light!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.540
Then you use
100,000 Volts, Pikachu!

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:18.590
Even 100,000 Volts
isn’t enough?

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:22.010
We need some stronger light
that can shine for longer...

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.050
Yeah.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.550
Denryu!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.760
Help us out!

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.140
We need your light
to find Sarunori!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:34.900
Denryu...

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.940
I mess things up
and get depressed a lot, too...

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.820
But I trust that if I don’t give up,
my dreams will come true!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:46.120
Maybe I’m not the most reliable person,
but I’ll do my best.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:49.280
So would you be up for
giving this another try with me?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.000
Almost got it!

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.930
Looking good, Denryu!

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.300
All right! Go for it!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.410
Go! Over there!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.790
Sarunori!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:43.510
Sheesh...
You had me so worried, Sarunori...

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.260
You really are like a lighthouse!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.800
Thank you!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.720
Denryu,
your light is a beacon for everyone!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.270
Denryu!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.560
Let’s go back to the Center!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:09.700
Mr. Hirota.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.950
Would you consider
letting us try again?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.040
Māmane... Denryu...

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.960
Of course.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.210
The equipment’s completely fixed, too.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.840
Come on, Denryu!

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:27.630
Go for it!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.400
We have an emergency!

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:42.940
Fiarrow2 deviated
from its trajectory!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.320
What happened?

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.400
An evasive maneuver
to avoid a meteorite.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:49.570
The sudden movement
didn’t give us time for attitude control.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.910
What does that mean?

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.160
It’s left its intended course.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.410
If it stays like this,
Fiarrow2 will never come home.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.540
Huh?

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:10.590
Māmane?

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.430
Yeah, this can work!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.470
Mr. Hirota!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.730
I have an idea!

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.480
An idea?

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:25.230
Right now, light from Kleiber Observatory
can still reach it.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.030
And by switching to Aeneas and Karna in turn,
we can pull it closer, bit by bit.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:35.490
Then if we send the re-entry signal
the moment it’s above Tokusane Space Center,

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.160
it should still be able to return!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.160
The math seems correct...

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.250
We’ll give it a try!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:43.750
Right!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.550
Contact the observatories!
Get ready!

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:47.750
Right!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.430
Kleiber, ready to illuminate!

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.390
Aeneas and Karna
will be ready at any second!

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.430
Commence operation!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.020
Let’s make this work!

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.520
<i>Right!</i>

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:13.110
It entered return trajectory!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:16.160
One minute until it’s above
Tokusane Space Center!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.160
Māmane, Denryu,
we’re counting on you!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.330
Right!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.540
Come on, Denryu!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:28.000
Send the light of hope
out into space!

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.550
Light, on!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.810
3, 2, 1...

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:40.720
Illuminate!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.310
Illuminating!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.320
The signal isn’t reaching!

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.570
Why?!

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:54.400
Is... the cloud cover too thick?

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.530
Denryu! We need more!

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.580
Pikachu!
We can help out, too!

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.000
100,000 Volts!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.470
Togedemaru,
use Shocking Prickles!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.300
You can help, too!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.600
Raichu, use Cheek Rub!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.530
<i>Go!</i>

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.790
Contact with Fiarrow2 confirmed!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.790
It’s entering the atmosphere!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:49.480
You did it, Māmane!

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:52.110
This is a feat
for the history books, no question!

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:54.150
W-Well... Yeah...

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.230
You did it too, Denryu!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:17.800
Māmane! I’ll be rooting for you
to become an astronaut!

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:18.840
Yeah!

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.890
Satoshi, Go...
You keep working toward your dreams, too!

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.090
Of course!

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.140
We’ll make them come true!

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:29.230
Until next time!

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:34.400
Seeing Māmane work
to reach his dream,

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.610
Satoshi and Go reaffirmed
their commitment to their dreams.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:42.860
There’s bound to be a bright light
illuminating their paths forward.

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.490
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:15.000
Those Yadon have yellow heads!

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.290
You’re right.

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.550
Too spicy!

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:22.880
What’s that?

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.760
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.970
Yadoking!
A Curry-ously Great Encounter!!
